    "body": "`claimed:` taking this - PR #645 already implements exactly this ask: every work-offset triad draws its Setup-pane name (`G54`, `Setup2/WCS`) just below its projected origin, the dimmed neutral world axes draw `World`, and an offset hidden by the Models-pane eye (or the world-axes toggle) loses its name with its lines. Pinned by `gizmo_tests` (world axes named `World` and dimmed like their lines, each triad named with its own offset name, the name stands at the origin rather than the tips, hidden offsets drop their names).\n\nThe PR cited #641 by mistake - that is the unrelated lathe grooving/parting bug, already fixed on main with its own decision doc (`docs/decisions/641-blade-corner.md`). The PR now closes this issue instead.\n",
